    "created_at": "2016-02-29T03:53:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-29T03:53:40Z",
    "body": "Hmm, OK, this is more complicated than it appears. Firefox follows the spec, but nobody else does. So maybe we should change this.\n\nhttp://jsbin.com/codoxe/1/edit?html,output (view console for results)\n- Firefox: 0, 0\n- Edge: 1, throws `\"Invalid argument error\"`, of type `Error` it seems!?\n- Chrome, Safari: 1, 1\n\nThe spec would allow two possible behaviors:\n- 0, 0 (current spec)\n- 1, throw IndexSizeError (if we changed it to \"limited to only non-negative numbers greater than zero\")\n\nSince there is no compatibility here, maybe we should change it to the latter, to better reflect the constraints of the table model?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
